Backport of the NETCMD_OPEN size header onto the pinned fujinet-firmware
(FUJINET_COMMIT in cmake/Dependencies.cmake).

MediaTypeROM::push_stream() has always known each stream's exact size -- it
takes expected_size and uses it to detect a short transfer -- but the OPEN
payload it sent was a single byte, the stream id, so the size never reached
the cart. Both cart implementations therefore drew the boot progress bar by
dividing bytes-so-far by a fixed 32768: a 13KB cart crawled to 41% and then
jumped to 100%, while a 232KB cart hit 99% after its first 32KB and stayed
there for the remaining 200KB.

Upstream fixed this by widening the OPEN payload to five bytes -- the stream
id followed by the total size, little-endian -- and consuming it on the
RP2040 side (bootmap_pct() in pico/intellivision/firmware/src/bootmap.c).
jzIntv's own receiver reads the same header (see tools/jzintv/
jzintv-fujinet.patch). This backports just the sender half onto the pinned
commit, which predates it, so the shipped desktop build actually sends what
the emulator now knows how to read.

Compatible in both directions by construction: a receiver that predates the
header reads data[0] for the stream id and ignores the rest, and a receiver
that expects it falls back to the old estimate when the payload is 1 byte.

u32le_t is unchanged at the pinned commit (include/global_types.h), so this
needs nothing else.

Drop this patch when FUJINET_COMMIT next moves to a revision that already
carries the change -- it is on fujinet-firmware master.

--- a/lib/media/rs232/diskTypeROM.cpp
+++ b/lib/media/rs232/diskTypeROM.cpp
@@ -57,12 +57,23 @@
 {
     uint8_t buf[DISK_SECTORBUF_SIZE];
 
-    uint8_t open_payload = (uint8_t)stream_id;
+    // OPEN payload is the stream id followed by the stream's total size as
+    // 4 little-endian bytes. The receiver needs the size to draw an exact
+    // progress bar -- without it there is nothing to divide by and the bar
+    // has to guess against a fixed constant. A receiver predating this
+    // reads data[0] and ignores the rest, so it stays compatible in both
+    // directions.
+    struct { uint8_t id; u32le_t size; } open_hdr;
+    static_assert(sizeof(open_hdr) == 5, "OPEN header must not be padded");
+    open_hdr.id = (uint8_t)stream_id;
+    open_hdr.size = expected_size;
+
     auto reply = SYSTEM_BUS.sendCommand(FUJI_DEVICEID_DBC, NETCMD_OPEN,
-                                        std::string(1, (char)open_payload));
+                                        std::string((const char *)&open_hdr, sizeof(open_hdr)));
     if (!reply || reply->command() != FUJICMD_ACK)
     {
-        Debug_printv("MediaTypeROM: failed to open DBC stream %u\n", stream_id);
+        Debug_printv("MediaTypeROM: failed to open DBC stream %u (%lu bytes)\n",
+                     stream_id, (unsigned long)expected_size);
         return false;
     }
 
